#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate spin-up and spin-down true A(k,omega) cubes on feature-aware grids.

Main change versus the Nomega-style builder:
- one common hybrid omega grid, dense near omega=0
- two spin-dependent k grids, each built from xi_sigma = k^2/m - mu_sigma
  so resolution is automatically concentrated near k_F,sigma

The spectral construction stays the same:
  A(k,w) = -C * Im[ 1 / (w - xi_k - Sigma^R(k,w) + i*eta_g) ]
with ImSigma from ``simga_test.imsigma_ret`` and ReSigma from KK reconstruction.

This file follows the simpler grid philosophy requested by the user, but it is
adapted to the current repo backend. The older ``Akw.*`` / ``FFLO_legacy``
modules are not present in this workspace, so we keep the grid logic and wire
it into the existing ``simga_test`` machinery that the rest of the pipeline
already uses.
"""

